ical/fire/rescue); Town of Alta Marshal''s Office (801) 742-3522 for local law enforcement; alert ski patrol on-mountain","hospital":"No in-canyon hospital - full-service ERs down-canyon in Salt Lake valley (~45 min-1 hr via SR-210, canyon-access permitting); verify nearest facility","malaria":"none","yellow_fever":"not required","activity_note":"ALTITUDE (base ~8,530 ft GENUINELY HIGH - higher than many resorts'' summits; summit ~11,068 ft; real AMS risk for sea-level arrivals - hydrate, ease alcohol, consider a valley night to acclimatise, descend if worsening); AVALANCHE life-safety spine (in-bounds patrolled/controlled; hike-to + backcountry severe) - Utah Avalanche Center (UAC) ''Salt Lake'' region - VERIFY exact zone (UAC page 403); beacon/probe/shovel + guide, never duck ropes; NO on-site cat/heli (Powderbird separate); SR-210 winter DEAD-END + traction law + UDOT avalanche closures + INTERLODGE (legal indoor confinement via Alta Central - follow Town/lodge instructions; exact ordinance verify); tree-wells; cold + intense high-elevation UV","fcdo":{"posture":"1","quotes":[],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/usa","read":"2026-08-20T14:47:42Z","page_updated":"2026-08-18T10:29:04+01:00","source_country":"usa","quotes_note":"not extracted by the join — a restricted-area clause is quoted by a human, never composed"},"posture":"book-freely"},"timing":{"peak":"Deep winter + storm/powder days (Christmas/NY, Presidents'' Week, any big storm cycle); heavy SL-valley day-trip traffic on powder mornings","shoulder":"early season (Dec), Jan midweek, long high-altitude spring (Apr)","green":"summer + fall (canyon quiets, no lift-served skiing) + Oct-Nov lull","booking_lead":"Christmas/NY + Presidents'' + the lodges (half-board, limited beds) 3-6 mo; storm-chasing powder trips opportunistic; Alta/Ikon passes by early summer (best-price deadline)","off_season_specials":"long spring skiing; midweek value; lodge half-board packages","event_peaks":"Christmas/NY, ML